01:13:44.720 --> 01:14:02.810
James Finley: really well-written code does not require a lot of comments, okay? So, again, if you use human-readable variable names, you break your code into individual lines, it's actually… it becomes very easy to see what's happening, so that you don't need excessive comments, okay?

450
01:14:03.370 --> 01:14:13.269
James Finley: You can always still add comments as you write your code, but, using, like I said, meaningful names goes a long way to making your code easy to understand.

